## Key Features of Source Code Security Reviews

Professional secure code review services may include static application security testing (SAST), manual code analysis, input validation checks, authentication and authorization reviews, cryptographic implementation assessments, and dependency security analysis.

Security specialists examine the code within an agreed scope and prepare a detailed report highlighting identified vulnerabilities, their severity, potential impact, and recommended fixes. Developers can use these findings to correct security issues and improve the application's overall resilience.

Conducting code reviews regularly throughout the software development lifecycle helps organizations identify problems before they reach production environments.

